WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.280
Two new polls put Brazil's runoff within two points with the presidency days away. This is Omni View, episode 208. Senator Flavio Bolsonaro and president Luis Ignacio Lula da Silva entered the October 25th runoff with a data-fola survey at 51% of valid votes for Bolsonaro and 49% for Lula. Mercopress reports that the result sits inside the polls margin of error, and that voter concerns over inflation and public safety have defined the closing week.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.060
The candidates have spent the final stretch trading positions on economic management

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:39.360
and security. Lula's campaign has emphasized social programs that reached millions during

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.940
his earlier terms. Bolsonaro's side highlights record low unemployment figures in some states

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.660
before the pandemic. Earlier surveys had shown a similar spread the previous week, indicating

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.040
little movement in the final stretch. Turnout among younger voters or in the northeast remains

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.200
the factor that could still decide the outcome.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.660
Lula supporters argue that expanding Bolsa Familia, a cash transfer program, and other payments

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.880
directly reduced extreme poverty rates in prior years. They say those transfers gave lower

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.560
income households a measurable buffer against price shocks. Bolsanaro's backers counter that his

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:21.020
administration's pension reform and pro-market measures laid groundwork for sustained private investment.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.020
They argue that reversing those steps would raise long-term borrowing costs for the state.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.380
People in each camp can see that external factors, such as global commodity prices, will

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.100
influence whichever candidate wins.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.100
The data-fold margin of error still allows either candidate to pull ahead if turnout

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.400
patterns and key regions break in their favor.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.760
Social programs on one ticket and labor market numbers on the other are the two records being

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.580
put in front of late deciding voters.

00:01:48.561 --> 00:01:55.161
Panama shook under a magnitude 7.6 earthquake, the United States Geological Survey, or USGS,

00:01:55.161 --> 00:02:01.881
the US agency that records magnitudes reported. The Hindu international notes that the shock arrived in

00:02:01.881 --> 00:02:07.841
daylight hours, which allowed rapid visual checks of structures. Visibly shaken residents of Panama

00:02:07.841 --> 00:02:12.721
City gathered outside buildings as authorities assessed impacts on infrastructure and homes.

00:02:13.401 --> 00:02:18.421
No immediate casualty figures have been confirmed. Officials are still compiling reports from

00:02:18.421 --> 00:02:24.041
outlying provinces, where the picture is less complete than in the capital. The event follows a pattern

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:29.101
of seismic activity along the Central American Subduction Zone, the plate boundary that has

00:02:29.101 --> 00:02:34.401
produced similar earthquakes in past decades. Residents described feeling strong shaking that

00:02:34.401 --> 00:02:40.261
prompted many to exit offices and homes immediately. In the capital and beyond, people are still waiting

00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:45.361
for a full account of what the shaking did to houses and roads. Engineers will complete building

00:02:45.361 --> 00:02:51.271
inspections and then release updated safety guidance for affected districts. Houthi missile strikes

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:55.991
hit areas near Adden, including the vicinity of the presidential palace, killing at least

00:02:55.991 --> 00:03:01.751
five people. Al Jazeera reports that Houthi forces have captured the port of Mocha, cutting

00:03:01.751 --> 00:03:07.171
one key resupply corridor for pro-government troops in western Tais. The attacks targeted

00:03:07.171 --> 00:03:12.491
supply routes used by government forces advancing under the dawn of Yemen operation. Government

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:17.911
spokesman State that alternative routes remain open and that operations will continue. Houthi

00:03:17.911 --> 00:03:21.811
Many military statements frame the strikes as responses to Saudi-backed movements.

00:03:22.391 --> 00:03:27.331
Colonel Wada Al-Dubayesh, spokesperson for the government-aligned Joint Forces on Yemen's

00:03:27.331 --> 00:03:32.451
West Coast, said military operations against the Houthis will continue despite the disruptions.

00:03:32.931 --> 00:03:37.351
Everything turns on whether those longer substitute roads can keep the offensive supplied.

00:03:37.971 --> 00:03:42.131
Government officials maintain that sustained pressure on Houthi positions will eventually

00:03:42.131 --> 00:03:46.091
restore control over the capital, Sana'a, seized in 2014.

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:51.331
Houthi representatives argue that territorial gains around TIE's demonstrate the limits

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:56.931
of external support for the Adin-based administration, and that further advances will force negotiations

00:03:56.931 --> 00:03:57.951
on their terms.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:03.231
The loss of MOCA has already forced government forces to rely on longer alternative supply

00:04:03.231 --> 00:04:06.371
lines, increasing vulnerability to further strikes.

00:04:07.274 --> 00:04:11.074
Prime Minister Takaichi made a ritual offering to Yasukuni Shrine.

00:04:11.694 --> 00:04:16.454
The Japan Times reports that the offering follows long-standing practice among some conservative

00:04:16.454 --> 00:04:16.874
of leaders.

00:04:17.554 --> 00:04:20.594
A ritual offering is a ceremonial gift sent to the shrine.

00:04:21.134 --> 00:04:23.514
It is not the same as walking the grounds in person.

00:04:24.154 --> 00:04:27.834
She is expected to skip a personal visit during the three-day autumn festival.

00:04:28.394 --> 00:04:33.674
That festival is a shinto observance, Japan's indigenous religious tradition, and it runs

00:04:33.674 --> 00:04:34.314
through Monday.

00:04:35.114 --> 00:04:38.334
Neighboring governments have previously criticized gestures of this kind.

00:04:38.874 --> 00:04:43.914
Their objection is that the shrine honors war-dead, including people convicted as war criminals.

00:04:43.914 --> 00:04:48.594
Domestic supporters view the same act as respect for those who died in service.

00:04:49.074 --> 00:04:53.254
The line being drawn this week is between a mailed tribute and a personal appearance at

00:04:53.254 --> 00:04:53.754
the Shrine.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:00.860
The European Central Bank or ECB, through President Christine Lagarde, urged Euro-Area governments

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.480
to exercise fiscal discipline as inflation pressures reappear.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.180
Investing.com India notes that Lagarde linked loose national budgets to the difficulty of

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.400
keeping inflation near the 2% target.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:18.220
it. Energy and food prices have shown renewed upward movement. Fiscal discipline here means

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:23.120
holding down national spending and borrowing while prices are under pressure. Some member

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.840
states have increased spending to offset higher living costs, while others have prioritized

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:33.360
debt reduction. The Euro area shares one interest rate policy, but each government still writes

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.940
its own budget. That split between national fiscal choices and a single monetary policy remains

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.380
at the center of the argument.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:46.180
Divergent national approaches can complicate the effort to keep prices stable across the currency union.

00:05:47.078 --> 00:05:53.098
Brent Crude, the International Oil Benchmark, touched $110 a barrel for the first time since May.

00:05:53.798 --> 00:05:59.698
Mercopress reports it settled at $109.86 after a 3.7% gain,

00:06:00.338 --> 00:06:08.238
and that West Texas Intermediate, or WTI, the US Benchmark rose 3.5% to $101.41.

00:06:08.238 --> 00:06:13.818
sense. Traders cited uncertainty over Russian diesel exports and tensions affecting red-sea

00:06:13.818 --> 00:06:18.938
shipping lanes. Market participants are weighing whether recent regional developments will reduce

00:06:18.938 --> 00:06:24.618
available supply in the coming months. Refiners and governments are monitoring inventory levels and

00:06:24.618 --> 00:06:30.298
alternative sourcing options. The close is the highest settlement since May 19th, and it reflects

00:06:30.298 --> 00:06:36.502
concerns that supply disruptions could persist. Amazon forest clearance is progress worth knowing,

00:06:36.502 --> 00:06:42.102
according to official data. Al Jazeera notes a 42 percent drop compared with the same period

00:06:42.102 --> 00:06:47.922
last year, the lowest level on record. The figures give President Lula measurable progress ahead

00:06:47.922 --> 00:06:53.062
of the runoff vote. Enforcement actions and satellite monitoring have contributed to the decline.

00:06:53.762 --> 00:06:58.282
Satellite monitoring in this setting means using orbiting imagery to spot new clearing,

00:06:58.742 --> 00:07:04.002
then sending teams to the ground. Previous administrations face criticism for weaker controls.

00:07:04.002 --> 00:07:09.242
goals. Current efforts include expanded field operations and international financing commitments.

00:07:09.682 --> 00:07:14.302
The main complication remains sustaining funding and coordination across multiple states

00:07:14.302 --> 00:07:20.202
and agencies. The drop provides a concrete benchmark for evaluating ongoing conservation measures.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.720
To really understand a Brazilian presidential runoff, you have to see the absolute majority

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:32.140
rule as a coalition machine, not a simple rematch. The Constitution written in 1988 after

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:37.780
military rule requires an absolute majority in the first round. Absolute majority means

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:43.020
more than half of the valid vote, not merely finishing first. If nobody clears that bar,

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:48.600
the system orders a second contest between only the top two finishers. The rule was introduced

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:54.300
to push candidates toward broader coalitions. In most recent cycles, no single candidate has

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:59.380
one outright on the first ballot, so the second round is the normal path, not an exception.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.180
That is where smaller parties become decisive.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:07.880
They can withhold or grant support in exchange for cabinet posts or written policy concessions.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.820
Coverage that treats a runoff as just another vote often skips this bargaining step.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:18.460
When a campaign claims it has momentum, the mechanism to test is whether eliminated rivals

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:20.820
have already pledged that second round support.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.720
Momentum without those pledges is still a first round left over.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.800
momentum with them is a governing coalition being assembled in public.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:33.700
Historical patterns show that second-round deals often set the cabinet's composition

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.760
and the legislative priorities of the incoming administration.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.840
Those bargains keep occurring because first-round knockouts have been rare under this design.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.020
The concrete thing to check before ballots are cast is whether either camp publishes formal

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.600
agreements with parties that finish third or fourth.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:54.840
Until those papers appear, the open trail is public statements from the eliminated candidates

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:55.440
themselves.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:00.940
Electoral court filings sit underneath the commentary, and they are the baseline that

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.880
secondary summaries can drift away from.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:07.900
Merkel Press reads this election cycle as a pocketbook and security contest.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:13.040
Al Jazeera's forest numbers read the same cycle as a test of environmental enforcement.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:19.240
Formal diplomatic responses from China or South Korea to the Yasukuni offering would, if

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.000
If they come, arrive in the coming days.

